James inquired about a closed form expression for the sum \( \sum_{t=0}^{T} e^{bt} \). I provided the formula for integer \( T \ge 0 \): 

\[
\sum_{t=0}^{T} e^{bt} = \frac{e^{b(T+1)}-1}{e^b-1}, \quad b \ne 0,
\]

and noted that for \( b=0 \), the sum equals \( T+1 \). Additionally, I mentioned a numerically convenient equivalent form for small \( b \):

\[
\sum_{t=0}^{T} e^{bt} = e^{bT/2}\,\frac{\sinh\!\left(b(T+1)/2\right)}{\sinh(b/2)}.
\] This concise response covered the closed-form solutions and alternative expressions based on different values of \( b \).
